STATEMENT OF CHANGES  (GNU GPL v3, section 5(a) and section 7)

The original work has been modified as follows:

1.  Renamed.  The software is distributed under the name "HMCL-DSH", not
    "HMCL" or "Hello Minecraft! Launcher", as required by the additional
    terms attached to HMCL under GNU GPL v3 section 7(c).

2.  Scope.  All functionality related to launching, installing or managing
    Minecraft has been removed, together with the corresponding source
    packages (game, download, auth, modpack, addon, schematic, nbt, java,
    launch, upgrade, terracotta, countly) and the associated user-interface
    pages.

3.  Purpose.  The application now launches and manages DeepSeek Harness
    (`dsh`) profiles and versions, which is implemented in the new
    `org.jackhuang.hmcl.dsh` package and the new user-interface pages under
    `org.jackhuang.hmcl.ui.dsh`.

4.  Retained.  The presentation layer -- the JavaFX window decorator, the
    component library, the animation helpers, the theme engine, the image
    pipeline, the asynchronous task engine, the localization framework and
    the general-purpose utilities -- is carried over from HMCL, keeping its
    original package names and its original copyright headers, which are
    preserved in full as required by GNU GPL v3 section 7(b).

5.  Removed.  The self-update mechanism (which used HMCL's own update server
    and signing key), the crash-reporting submission path, the Countly
    package name, the Terracotta integration and every hard-coded reference
    to HMCL's servers, documentation, community links and branding have been
    removed or replaced.

6.  Platform.  Only Linux is supported.  Windows- and macOS-specific code
    paths are not maintained.

The full source code of this modified version is available from the project
repository in which this notice is distributed.

